# Keep sources.html up to date

**Parent gate:** also follow `sync-site-downloadables-and-sources.mdc` (website edits require downloadables + sources in the same task).

Whenever you add, update, or remove **news stories, citations, dossiers, patents, speech visuals, or other distributables** on this site, **update `sources.html` in the same task**. The bibliography and the pages that cite sources must not drift.

## What belongs in sources.html

| Kind | Where in sources |
|---|---|
| External article / court / gov / vendor URL used on any `*.html` page | Matching topic panel (National liability, Tennessee, open-streams, patent, CEO, etc.) or main bibliography |
| On-site civic PDFs and JSON catalogs | **On-site primary documents** (+ topic panel if relevant). Case catalogs are JSON + searchable tables, not master-database PDFs. |
| Dossier lookup widgets | Same dossier line, plus the searchable-table link (`national.html#cancel-lookup`, `#misuse-lookup`, `#wrongful-lookup`) |
| Dossier tally snapshot | On-site primary documents → `docs/dossier-tallies.json` |
| Wayback archive catalog | On-site primary documents → `docs/source-archives.json` |
| Local evidence stills shown on dossier pages or used as speech visuals (Condor, patent pages, Oshkosh exhibit) | Matching topic panel (open-streams, patent, National / CEO) with asset path links |
| Council speech catalog / PDF set | On-site primary documents → speech picker / `docs/speeches/` / `Council_Speeches_3min.json` |
| TPRA request templates | On-site primary documents → `docs/TPRA_Request_Templates.json` / `records.html#foia` |

## Checklist before finishing a content change

1. Diff new `https://` links on touched pages against `sources.html`.
2. Snapshot those new URLs on the Wayback Machine and upsert `docs/source-archives.json` (see `archive-sources-on-wayback.mdc`).
3. If you added `docs/*` or `assets/flock-*` / `assets/speech-visuals/*` exhibits, list them (or the parent folder + key files) under On-site primary documents or the topic panel.
4. Prefer primary URLs already cited on the page; do not invent secondary sources just to pad the bibliography.
5. Note in the reply that sources were synced (or explicitly say a link was intentionally omitted and why).

## OK to omit (say so if relevant)

- Pure navigation / contact portals (city email forms, “find your representative”, Maps deep-links for meeting addresses)
- Shopping links for consumer doorbells / cameras on printables how-tos
- Share-button endpoints and video thumbnail CDNs
- `*-print.jpg` crops when the matching full PNG is already listed
- Dossier-internal Case_ID URLs already covered by the JSON catalog / searchable-table footnote
- Printables flyer PDFs already catalogued on `printables.html` (optional cross-link is fine)

## Do not

- Ship new national/TN/Flock catalog cites without a sources.html entry
- Leave patent / Condor / Oshkosh exhibit assets used in speeches unlisted when they are primary evidence
- Reintroduce or link the retired master-database PDFs (`Flock_Safety_ALPR_Misuse_Master_Database.pdf`, `Flock_Municipal_Cancellations_Database.pdf`, `AI_Wrongful_Enforcement_Database.pdf`)
